# The backend a production build talks to. Baked in at build time, so this file
# is the difference between a deployed app and one quietly calling localhost:
# a build without it falls back to http://localhost:8091 (see src/api.ts) and
# every screen sits on "the backend may be waking up" forever. It shipped that
# way once.
VITE_JOBPULSE_API=https://jobpulse-68gm.onrender.com

# VITE_JOBPULSE_VAPID is deliberately not set here, because the key is not
# recorded anywhere in this repo and guessing it would be worse than omitting
# it: push.ts passes `vapidKey: VAPID || undefined`, so Firebase falls back to
# the project's default web push certificate, which is what the first working
# end-to-end delivery used. Server-side sends never involve it — the poller
# authenticates with the service account — so this only affects a browser
# subscribing for the first time. To pin it, copy the public key from Firebase
# console → Cloud Messaging → Web Push certificates and add it here.
